          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "<p><strong>The University of California and California State University campuses no longer require SAT or ACT scores for admission.</strong></p><p>If you plan to apply to a private university, check that school's admission requirements. Some private colleges still require or recommend a test score.</p><h3>Registering for the SAT</h3><ol><li>Go to <a href=\"https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/sat/registration\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">satsuite.collegeboard.org</a> and create a College Board account, or sign in to an existing one.</li><li>Choose &quot;Register&quot; and pick your test date and centre.</li><li>Follow the directions and read each question carefully.</li></ol><h4>While you register</h4><ul><li>Answer the questions about your academic and personal interests. College Board uses them to connect you with colleges and scholarship opportunities.</li><li>Wait to enter a fee-waiver code until the form asks for it. See your counsellor to find out if you qualify for one.</li></ul><h3>Sending your scores</h3><ul><li>Colleges do not receive your scores automatically. You choose the recipients.</li><li>Every registration includes four free score sends.</li><li>Order your free sends no later than nine days after the test date.</li><li>After nine days, each score report costs $12.00 per school.</li><li>Every college sets its own score deadline. Check each admission website so your scores arrive in time.</li></ul><h4>Cal State and UC applicants</h4><ul><li>Cal State campuses are test-free. You do not send SAT or ACT scores with a Cal State Apply application.</li><li>UC campuses are also test-free for admission. If you send scores to one UC campus, every UC campus can see them.</li></ul><h3>When should you take the SAT?</h3><ul><li>Take it in May or June of your junior year.</li><li>Leave room for one or two retakes in the autumn of your senior year.</li><li>For most colleges, the December test date of senior year is the practical cut-off.</li></ul><p>Not sure where to apply yet? Use <a href=\"https://bigfuture.collegeboard.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BigFuture</a> to explore colleges and build a list.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
